WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.854
We shouldn't back away from

00:00:01.854 --> 00:00:03.750
discussing  polarizing issues,

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:06.464
even if it's with people 
who disagree&nbsp;with us.

00:00:06.464 --> 00:00:08.906
By having these conversations,

00:00:08.906 --> 00:00:10.594
you will gain insight into people

00:00:10.594 --> 00:00:12.851
who think&nbsp;differently
than you do.

00:00:12.851 --> 00:00:14.874
Sure, it's uncomfortable,

00:00:14.874 --> 00:00:17.160
and yeah, I'd probably 
agree that we don't

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.849
change our minds 
most of the time.

00:00:19.849 --> 00:00:21.698
But we can better understand

00:00:21.698 --> 00:00:22.853
opposing perspectives,

00:00:23.358 --> 00:00:25.013
which can help us 
to better advocate

00:00:25.013 --> 00:00:26.686
for our own beliefs.

00:00:26.686 --> 00:00:29.871
Just talk about something
 that’s&nbsp;uncomfortable,

00:00:29.871 --> 00:00:32.845
unconventional and 
meaningful to you.

00:00:32.845 --> 00:00:34.000
And most importantly,

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.802
do it with the intent&nbsp;
to listen and learn,

00:00:36.802 --> 00:00:39.080
not to win and not to agree.

